# /etc/pf.anchors/com.user.ollama-serve
#
# FEAT-1021 — scope pop ollama to LAN + Tailscale CGNAT only.
#
# pop's LaunchAgent (`com.user.ollama-serve`) binds 0.0.0.0:11434 so the
# cluster can reach it via the coredns-custom ConfigMap
# (k8s/coredns-custom-configmap.yaml) which resolves
# ollama-pop.homelab.local → 192.168.1.6. The WAN path is already closed
# by the router, but Tailscale and LAN scanners can still hit 11434.
# This anchor makes the bind truly private: only the LAN (cluster nodes,
# on-LAN MacBook) and the Tailscale CGNAT range (100.64.0.0/10) can reach
# the listener. Everything else is blocked.
#
# Install (one-time, on pop):
#
#   sudo cp mac/pf/com.user.ollama-serve.anchor /etc/pf.anchors/com.user.ollama-serve
#   sudo chmod 644 /etc/pf.anchors/com.user.ollama-serve
#
# Wire into /etc/pf.conf (append after the OS-default anchors, before any
# closing brace):
#
#   load anchor "com.user.ollama-serve" from "/etc/pf.anchors/com.user.ollama-serve"
#
# Then load + verify:
#
#   sudo pfctl -f /etc/pf.conf
#   sudo pfctl -e            # enable if not already
#   sudo pfctl -a com.user.ollama-serve -sr   # anchor rules are NOT
#                                             # in the main ruleset —
#                                             # query the anchor directly
#
# Rollback:
#
#   sudo pfctl -a com.user.ollama-serve -F all
#   sudo rm /etc/pf.anchors/com.user.ollama-serve
#   # And remove the `load anchor` line from /etc/pf.conf
#
# See mac/docs/ollama-pop-fw.md for the full rationale and the
# socketfilterfw alternative (binary allow, no subnet scoping).

# pop's `com.user.ollama-serve` LaunchAgent binds IPv6 `*:11434` (dual-
# stack — also accepts IPv4-mapped traffic), so the rules must cover both
# `inet` (IPv4) and `inet6` (IPv6). The cluster reaches pop on IPv4
# (192.168.1.6 LAN + 100.64.0.0/10 Tailscale CGNAT); Tailscale peers
# also come in over IPv6 on the specific `utun9` interface using the
# well-known Tailnet ULA prefix `fd7a:115c:a1e0::/48`. (The other
# `utun*` interfaces on macOS are link-local only and belong to other
# tunnels — WARP, Mullvad, etc. — so we scope the Tailscale rule to
# `utun9` to avoid matching them.)
#
# IMPORTANT: do NOT use `utun* inet6 from 100.64.0.0/10` — pf will fail
# with "rule expands to no valid combination" because 100.64.0.0/10 has
# no IPv6 members. (Lesson learned the hard way on 2026-06-30.)

# Allow inbound TCP 11434 from LAN (cluster nodes + on-LAN MacBook), both v4 and v6.
pass in quick on en0 inet  proto tcp from 192.168.1.0/24 to any port 11434
pass in quick on en0 inet6 proto tcp from fe80::/10        to any port 11434

# Allow inbound TCP 11434 from Tailscale (off-LAN MacBook, phones).
pass in quick on utun9 inet  proto tcp from 100.64.0.0/10   to any port 11434
pass in quick on utun9 inet6 proto tcp from fd7a:115c:a1e0::/48 to any port 11434

# Block everything else that would hit the LAN-side bind, both v4 and v6.
block in quick on en0 inet  proto tcp to any port 11434
block in quick on en0 inet6 proto tcp to any port 11434
